1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,226
तुम अभी तक cartoon देखती हो?

2
00:00:01,226 --> 00:00:05,266
If I had a rupee for every time someone said this to me, I could probably afford a

3
00:00:05,266 --> 00:00:06,846
Japan trip by now, maybe.

4
00:00:06,846 --> 00:00:14,166
[laughs] I don't wanna date myself because I'm just a younger millennial, but anime was not really cool when

5
00:00:14,166 --> 00:00:19,206
I was growing up. Today, if you go out wearing a Gojo T-shirt, you can get away with it.

6
00:00:19,206 --> 00:00:23,946
But back then, if you told someone you liked anime, people assumed that your social life was a

7
00:00:23,946 --> 00:00:26,146
B- and that you were a loser.

8
00:00:26,146 --> 00:00:31,626
Also, unfortunately, I have this condition, when I love something, it becomes 90% of my personality.

9
00:00:31,626 --> 00:00:33,006
So there was no hiding it.

10
00:00:33,006 --> 00:00:36,306
I was watching anime even if it was considered uncool back then.

11
00:00:36,306 --> 00:00:41,006
Looking back, I think I did it because anime did something much bigger for me. It kind of

12
00:00:41,006 --> 00:00:44,906
raised me. I spent a major part of my childhood in the Middle East, so when I moved to

13
00:00:44,906 --> 00:00:46,586
Pakistan, everything was very different.

14
00:00:46,586 --> 00:00:50,026
Culture, traditions, relationships, and even language.

15
00:00:50,026 --> 00:00:54,366
I'm a Pathan, and I learned Pashto pretty late in life, so you know it was tough. And

16
00:00:54,366 --> 00:00:58,946
when you're a kid trying to fit into a place, you try and look for familiar things.

17
00:00:58,946 --> 00:01:03,226
For me, it was anime, and I loved it so much. But how did they help me? One

18
00:01:03,226 --> 00:01:06,666
Piece taught me something about ambition that I still believe to this day.

19
00:01:06,666 --> 00:01:09,426
Luffy wants something absolutely ridiculous.

20
00:01:09,426 --> 00:01:11,386
He announces it to everyone.

21
00:01:11,386 --> 00:01:17,166
Everyone laughs at him, but he proceeds anyway. As someone who has repeatedly had ideas that made people

22
00:01:17,166 --> 00:01:21,326
go, "Mm, why?" I think that philosophy has been really useful.

23
00:01:21,326 --> 00:01:24,286
And as the oldest child, Luffy also taught me leadership.

24
00:01:24,286 --> 00:01:28,426
You forgive, encourage, protect, and cheer for your people no matter what.

25
00:01:28,426 --> 00:01:30,606
Digimon taught me all I know about friendship.

26
00:01:30,606 --> 00:01:37,546
Taichi and Yamato could fight, disagree, and have completely different personalities, but whenever things got serious, they showed up,

27
00:01:37,546 --> 00:01:42,246
always together. Pokémon taught me about evolution before I even understood evolution.

28
00:01:42,246 --> 00:01:45,346
You don't really need to be a mystic animal to understand that.

29
00:01:45,346 --> 00:01:51,466
Change is inevitable and possibly the best thing to experience as a human being, because sometimes becoming the next

30
00:01:51,466 --> 00:01:54,686
version of yourself is the whole point. And then there was Beyblade.

31
00:01:54,686 --> 00:02:01,486
Beyblade taught me and an entire generation about ambition, competition, and also learning how to lose without becoming

32
00:02:01,486 --> 00:02:05,806
the villain of the next arc. These shows were my friends before I actually made friends.

33
00:02:05,806 --> 00:02:08,546
And eventually, Pakistan stopped feeling so unfamiliar.

34
00:02:08,546 --> 00:02:13,406
I found my people, I found my confidence, and I also learned the language.

35
00:02:13,406 --> 00:02:18,026
Well, mostly. And yes, I still watch anime. It wasn't just a phase. So if you're an anime

36
00:02:18,026 --> 00:02:22,626
fan as well, tell me what show got you into it, and what shows are you watching right now?

37
00:02:22,626 --> 00:02:27,146
Because I really need some recommendations for character development, obviously.

